<title>CHINA: DBS HK branch FRCD raised to HK$450 mln.</title>
<headline>DBS HK branch FRCD raised to HK$450 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Development Bank of Singapore Hongkong branch's floating-rate certificates of deposit issue has been increased to HK$450 million from HK$300 million, arranger Societe Generale Asia said on Monday.</p>
<p>The three-year certificates were issued at par to float at 22 basis points over the three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate. With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is 27 basis points.</p>
<p>Six financial institutions in addition to the arranger joined the syndication.</p>
<p>The payment date is August 22.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
